wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page(
 p_id=>3
,p_name=>'How to Use'
,p_alias=>'HOW-TO-USE'
,p_step_title=>'Navigation Studio - How to Use'
,p_autocomplete_on_off=>'OFF'
,p_inline_css=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'.nvs-Doc { max-width: 60rem; line-height: 1.7; }',
'.nvs-Doc h3 { margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.125rem; }',
'.nvs-Doc h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }',
'.nvs-Doc ol, .nvs-Doc ul { padding-inline-start: 1.25rem; margin: .25rem 0 .75rem; }',
'.nvs-Doc li { margin: .2rem 0; }',
'.nvs-Doc pre { margin: .5rem 0 1rem; padding: .875rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 8px; background: #1f2329; color: #e6edf3; font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.55; }',
'.nvs-Doc p code, .nvs-Doc li code, .nvs-Doc td code { padding: .05rem .35rem; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(127,127,127,.14); font-size: .8125rem; }',
'.nvs-Doc table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; font-size: .875rem; }',
'.nvs-Doc th, .nvs-Doc td { padding: .45rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ut-component-border-color, #e4e7ec); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }',
'.nvs-Doc th { font-weight: 700; opacity: .8; }',
'.nvs-Doc td:first-child { font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }'))
,p_step_template=>4073832297226169690
,p_page_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_page_is_public_y_n=>'Y'
,p_protection_level=>'C'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(11855326663985849)
,p_plug_name=>'How to Use'
,p_static_id=>'breadcrumb'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-BreadcrumbRegion--useBreadcrumbTitle'
,p_component_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_plug_template=>2532939663579242476
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_01'
,p_plug_item_display_point=>'ABOVE'
,p_location=>null
,p_menu_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(11847467112985824)
,p_plug_source_type=>'NATIVE_BREADCRUMB'
,p_menu_template_id=>4073839682315169711
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(11855426696985849)
,p_plug_name=>'Use Navigation Studio in Your Own App'
,p_static_id=>'guide'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_plug_template=>4073835273271169698
,p_plug_display_sequence=>20
,p_plug_item_display_point=>'ABOVE'
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<div class="nvs-Doc">',
'<h3>1. Get Navigation Studio into your workspace</h3>',
'<ol>',
'  <li>Download <code>navigation-studio.sql</code> from <a href="https://github.com/HashaamShoukat/apex-navigation-studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</li>',
'  <li><strong>App Builder &gt; Import</strong>, install it with any application ID. No database objects; APEX 26.1 or later.</li>',
'</ol>',
'',
'<h3>2. Copy the templates into your application</h3>',
'<p>In <em>your</em> application: <strong>Shared Components &gt; Templates &gt; Create &gt; List &gt; As a Copy of an Existing Template</strong>, copy from <strong>Navigation Studio</strong> and pick the ones you need (tick <em>Subscribe</em> for late'
||'r updates):</p>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>Template</th><th>Use it for</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Side Navigation</td><td>The side navigation menu (a copy of Universal Theme''s Side Navigation Menu).</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Top Navigation</td><td>The top navigation menu (a copy of Top Navigation Menu).</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Navigation Bar</td><td>The navigation bar - user menu, notifications, help. It takes the colours of the menu templates.</td></tr>',
'</table>',
'<p>Each template loads its CSS from a static file, which the copy does not bring along. Upload the matching files to <strong>Shared Components &gt; Static Application Files</strong> in your application, in a directory named <code>navigation-studio</c'
||'ode>. Download them from Navigation Studio''s own Static Application Files, or from <code>apexlang/shared-components/static-files/navigation-studio</code> on GitHub.</p>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>Template</th><th>File</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Side Navigation</td><td><code>navigation-studio/side-nav.css</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Top Navigation</td><td><code>navigation-studio/top-nav.css</code></td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Modern Navigation Bar</td><td><code>navigation-studio/nav-bar.css</code></td></tr>',
'</table>',
'<p>To share one copy between several applications, upload them as Static Workspace Files instead and change <code>&#35;APP_FILES&#35;</code> to <code>&#35;WORKSPACE_FILES&#35;</code> in the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> at the start of each template''s <e'
||'m>Before List Entries</em>.</p>',
'',
'<h3>3. Switch your application to them</h3>',
'<ol>',
'  <li><strong>Shared Components &gt; User Interface Attributes &gt; Navigation Menu</strong>: List Template = <strong>Modern Side Navigation</strong> (or Modern Top Navigation with Position = Top), then the <strong>Template Options</strong> you chose'
||' in the Designer.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Navigation Bar</strong>: List Template = <strong>Modern Navigation Bar</strong> and its Template Options.</li>',
'</ol>',
'<p>The Designer gives you the options and the same settings as APEXlang for <code>application.apx</code>. Nothing else changes: the templates keep Universal Theme''s markup and ids, so the collapse button, keyboard, remembered state and phone overlay '
||'work as before.</p>',
'',
'<h3>4. Make the most of the list</h3>',
'<table>',
'  <tr><th>In the list</th><th>What it does</th></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Label <code>Inbox [12]</code></td><td>A badge with 12 (side and top menu; Universal Theme''s own syntax). Use a substitution for a live count: <code>Inbox [&amp;P0_UNREAD.]</code>.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Attribute 3</td><td>Side menu: a section heading above the entry. Type the heading (e.g. <em>Reports</em>) in the entry''s <strong>User Defined Attributes &gt; 3</strong> (Shared Components &gt; Lists &gt; your list &gt; the entry). It is sh'
||'own above that entry and starts a new group; when the menu is collapsed it becomes a divider line. The demo menu''s WORKSPACE, SALES, INSIGHTS and ADMIN, and the NAVIGATION STUDIO and DEMOS headings of this app''s own menu, are made this way.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Navigation bar: Attribute 1</td><td>The badge value of a navigation bar entry.</td></tr>',
'  <tr><td>Navigation bar: Attribute 2</td><td>List item CSS classes. <code>ns-User</code> shows the initials of the label in a round avatar (option User Avatar); <code>icon-only</code> and <code>no-icon</code> work as in Universal Theme.</td></tr>',
'</table>',
'',
'<h3>5. What the options do</h3>',
'<ul>',
'  <li><strong>Menu Search</strong> - a field above the side menu that finds every entry, sub-levels too. <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> (<kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd>) or <kbd>/</kbd> opens it.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Search Button</strong> (navigation bar, off by default) - a button that opens that search field. It shows only while the side menu is collapsed or hidden; when the menu is expanded the field is already in view.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Sub-menus: Flyout</strong> - sub-levels open in a panel beside the menu instead of expanding in place: on hover, with a tap on the arrow, or with the Right arrow key (Up / Down move inside it, Left or Escape closes it). It works on the '
||'collapsed icon rail too. Phones always expand in place.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Tooltips When Collapsed</strong> - the entry''s name next to the icon on the collapsed rail (mouse and keyboard).</li>',
'  <li><strong>Phone Bottom Bar</strong> - on phones the first four entries and a Menu button sit in a bar at the bottom, in reach of the thumb.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Header: Match the Menu</strong> - the header bar takes the menu''s colours; <em>Keep Theme Header</em> leaves it to your theme style.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Color Scheme</strong> - the menu and header only; your theme style keeps the content. Midnight and Terminal are always dark.</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>Texts can be translated with the text messages <code>MODERN_NAV.SEARCH</code>, <code>MODERN_NAV.NO_MATCH</code>, <code>MODERN_NAV.MENU</code> and <code>MODERN_NAV.QUICK_LINKS</code>.</p>',
'',
'<h3>6. Good to know</h3>',
'<ul>',
'  <li>The JavaScript travels with each template; the CSS is the one static file per template from step 2 (a list template''s inline CSS holds only 4,000 bytes). A <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> at the start of <em>Before List Entries</em> loads it before t'
||'he menu is drawn, so the menu never shows its default colours first. Keep the small script in <em>After List Entries</em>: it applies the look before the menu is drawn.</li>',
'  <li>The source is generated from <code>apexlang/_src</code> on GitHub - edit there and run <code>node _src/build.mjs</code> rather than editing the minified JavaScript in the template.</li>',
'  <li>Users who prefer reduced motion get no animations; Windows high-contrast mode is respected.</li>',
'</ul>',
'</div>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
end;
/
